cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "Shao"
    given-names: "Shoupeng"
    alias: "魔法徽章"
title: "SUI: Semantic Unified Interface — A Semantic Encoding Protocol for Large Language Models"
version: 6.7
date-released: "2026-08-27"
url: "https://gitee.com/mofahuizhang/SUI"
license:
  - "MulanPSL-2.0"
  - "CC-BY-NC-4.0"
abstract: "SUI (Semantic Unified Interface) is a formal semantic encoding protocol designed with large language models as the primary reader. It inserts a layer of formalized semantic addresses between natural language and model inference, enabling precise concept addressing rather than probabilistic disambiguation. SUI is grounded in the CART/CCT/CSMT tri-framework and maintains a hard-encoding/soft-routing relationship with SCION."
keywords:
  - "semantic encoding"
  - "large language models"
  - "semantic addressing"
  - "cognitive coding theory"
  - "AI intermediate representation"
  - "context state"
  - "semantic phase dynamics"
